# hipaa-compliance-engine

Path: src/pages/HIPAACheckPage.tsx (questions + calculateResults), src/components/assessment/AssessmentEngine.tsx (UI + localStorage save)

This is a client-side questionnaire, not a live HIPAA control validator. Results persist in localStorage under hipaa-assessments. Tier limits use useTierLimit.

## Question set (10 domains)

Each question has four options scored 0–5. Max score = 50. Percentage = round(score / 50 * 100).

1. risk-assessment — Security Rule §164.308(a)(1), §164.306(a)
2. policies-procedures — Security Rule §164.316(a), Privacy Rule §164.530(i)
3. employee-training — Security Rule §164.308(a)(5), Privacy Rule §164.530(b)
4. encryption — Security Rule §164.312(a)(2)(iv), §164.312(e)(2)(ii)
5. access-controls — Security Rule §164.308(a)(4), §164.312(a)(1) (shown in questionMapping)
6. business-associates — Privacy Rule §164.502(e), Security Rule §164.308(b)
7. incident-response — Security Rule §164.308(a)(6), Breach Notification §164.408
8. audit-logs — Security Rule §164.312(b)
9. device-security — Security Rule §164.310(d), §164.312(a)(2)(iii)
10. emergency-access — Security Rule §164.312(a)(2)(ii), §164.308(a)(7)

Question text and options go through i18n keys under hipaa_assessment. Recommendations inside calculateResults() are hardcoded English.

## Scoring

Equal weight: selected option.value summed. There is no 40/35/25 technical/administrative/physical split in this page.

Low answers (none / never / none implemented) emit high-priority recommendations; partial answers emit medium; emergency-access gaps are medium/low.

## Related engines

- RansomwareAssessment uses the same AssessmentEngine
- EnhancedAssessmentEngine rolls HIPAA + dependencies + continuity from localStorage; its ransomware score is a heuristic

